# Copy these into Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables
# (Production and Preview as needed). Do not commit real tokens.
#
# Recommended: one Vercel project with Services (see repo vercel.json + DEPLOYMENT.md).
# Dashboard: Framework Preset = Services, Root Directory = repo root or gui (never gui/frontend).

# Parquet data: repo data/ is NOT on Vercel’s filesystem. The API loads slices from Blob when set:
# Required for API cold-start hydration from Blob (origin only, no path):
# BLOB_PARQUET_BASE_URL=https://xxxx.public.blob.vercel-storage.com

# Required if the Blob store is private (same token as uploads):
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=vercel_blob_rw_...

# Same-origin API (frontend + FastAPI on Vercel): do NOT set, or leave empty:
# VITE_API_URL=
